    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c952dc73_5e0788bc",
        "filename": "driver/ln9310.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 433,
      "author": {
        "id": 1451837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-27T04:21:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this I2C command is sent (i.e. `LN9310_STARTUP_STANDBY_EN\u003d0`) and then the timeout is checked and fails, the only way to undo the command would be to send another I2C command (`LN9310_STARTUP_STANDBY_EN\u003d1`), but in that case what would guarantee that the new command would get sent in a fixed time?  \n\nThe point of the timeout is to prevent this I2C command from getting sent to the LN9310 if too much time (i.e. \u003e 100 ms) has elapsed since the previous I2C command occurred.  The previous I2C command disables the Cfly precharge, so if ln9310 doesn\u0027t try to startup quickly, the Cfly can be discharged too much prior to startup which could cause problems.\n\nIs there a way to setup the I2C operation (i.e. chip, address data) but not trigger it getting sent and then make the trigger conditional on having not timed out yet?",
      "parentUuid": "6d8a2890_e2fc94c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 431,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 433,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "789389c3230653ce59159a46edb72e515de36a31",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "943b6664_e4c15dc5",
        "filename": "driver/ln9310.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-26T22:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the else case? retry it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 434,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 434,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "789389c3230653ce59159a46edb72e515de36a31",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74404e1f_d4089ec8",
        "filename": "driver/ln9310.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1451837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-27T04:21:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the timeout occurs and `LN9310_STARTUP_STANDBY_EN` is not set to 0, then the entire `ln9310_init()` function should be retried.  I didn\u0027t put an else statement because I thought that if the ln9310 never receives this final command, then it will never enter switching and the higher level `set_system_power` will fail when it doesn\u0027t see `ln9310_power_good`.  I think maybe the retry should be initiated at that higher level (i.e. `set_system_power`) or somewhere similar.  What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "943b6664_e4c15dc5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 434,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 434,
        "endChar": 2
      },
